{title: Jesus, I Come}
{artist: William T. Sleeper / George C. Stebbins}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: A}
{tempo: 124}
{time: 6/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Gospel Hymns No. 5, edited by \tIra D. Sankey, James McGranahan & George C. Stebbins (Cincinnati, Ohio; New York ; Chicago: John Church/ Biglow & Main, 1887), #)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[A]Out of my bondage, [D]sorrow, and [A]night,
[A]Jesus, [E7]I come, Jesus, I [A]come;
[A]Into Thy freedom, [D]gladness, and [A]light,
[A]Jesus, I come__[E7]__ to [A]Thee;
[D]Out of my sickness, [A]into Thy health,
[E]Out of my want and [B7]into Thy__[E7]__ wealth,
[A]Out of my sin and [D]into Thy[A]self,
[A]Jesus, I come__[E7]__ to [A]Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[A]Out of my shameful [D]failure and [A]loss,
[A]Jesus, [E7]I come, Jesus, I [A]come;
[A]Into the glorious [D]gain of Thy [A]cross,
[A]Jesus, I come__[E7]__ to [A]Thee.
[D]Out of earth’s sorrows [A]into Thy balm,
[E]Out of life’s storms and [B7]into Thy__[E7]__ calm,
[A]Out of distress to [D]jubilant [A]psalm,
[A]Jesus, I come__[E7]__ to [A]Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[A]Out of unrest and [D]arrogant [A]pride,
[A]Jesus, [E7]I come, Jesus, I [A]come;
[A]Into Thy blessèd [D]will to a[A]bide,
[A]Jesus, I come__[E7]__ to [A]Thee.
[D]Out of myself to [A]dwell in Thy love,
[E]Out of despair into [B7]raptures a__[E7]__bove,
[A]Upward for aye on [D]wings like a [A]dove,
[A]Jesus, I come__[E7]__ to [A]Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[A]Out of the fear and [D]dread of the [A]tomb,
[A]Jesus, [E7]I come, Jesus, I [A]come;
[A]Into the joy and [D]light of Thy [A]throne,
[A]Jesus, I come__[E7]__ to [A]Thee.
[D]Out of the depths of [A]ruin untold,
[E]Into the peace of Thy [B7]sheltering__[E7]__ fold,
[A]Ever Thy glorious [D]face to be[A]hold,
[A]Jesus, I come__[E7]__ to [A]Thee.
{end_of_verse}
